You store it as "Zap", not "Recurrent Zap". I think whatever you did for the reference either broke it or I never noticed.
Evolution cards have their own name, aka "Recurrent Zap". They reference the card that is parsed from the alias: "alias: Evo: Zap" -> you parse Zap from here, as well as from the evolve ability: "<kw-0><nospellcheck><key>Evolve Spell: <param-name>Zap;</param-name></key></nospellcheck></kw-0> " -> you parse Zap. But that reference is a completely separate card that should be reffed, not the actual name of the evolution. I told you as new info that if the base card ref doesn't exist in the db yet, in the Related Cards section in the UI you should print a "(missing)" if the base is not in the db yet. You should do so for any related card that's missing, similar to the "stub"/"no definition yet" texts for keyword (if it's there, sorry but I can't check, as now the evos basically ref themselves, the app is really broken)

It used to work, but whatever you did now broke it. Please fix it.